# WN22-SO-000040: Windows Server 2022 built-in guest account must be renamed.
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: medium
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-so-000040-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `high`

    title `Windows Server 2022 built-in guest account must be renamed.`
    description `The built-in guest account is a well-known user account on all Windows systems and, as initially installed, does not require a password. This can allow access to system resources by unauthorized users. Renaming this account to an unidentified name improves the protection of this account and the system.`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,medium,security-option,security-policy,ksi-cmt-lmc,ksi-cmt-rmv,ksi-mla-evc,ksi-svc-acm`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-CMT-LMC,KSI:KSI-CMT-RMV,KSI:KSI-MLA-EVC,KSI:KSI-SVC-ACM,NIST-800-53:CM-6`
    control_objective `KSI-CMT-LMC,KSI-CMT-RMV,KSI-MLA-EVC,KSI-SVC-ACM`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration >> Windows Settings >> Security Settings >> Local Policies >> Security Options >> Accounts: Rename guest account to a name other than "Guest".`

    component_id `comp-windows-security-policy`

    impl_KSI_CMT_LMC `Windows Server implements KSI-CMT-LMC by enforcing NewGuestName per the STIG (Built-in Guest account must be renamed (NewGuestName != "Guest").). The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`
    impl_KSI_CMT_RMV `Windows Server implements KSI-CMT-RMV by enforcing NewGuestName per the STIG (Built-in Guest account must be renamed (NewGuestName != "Guest").). The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`
    impl_KSI_MLA_EVC `Windows Server implements KSI-MLA-EVC by enforcing NewGuestName per the STIG (Built-in Guest account must be renamed (NewGuestName != "Guest").). The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`
    impl_KSI_SVC_ACM `Windows Server implements KSI-SVC-ACM by enforcing NewGuestName per the STIG (Built-in Guest account must be renamed (NewGuestName != "Guest").). The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`
    impl_CM_6 `Windows Server implements CM-6 by enforcing NewGuestName per the STIG (Built-in Guest account must be renamed (NewGuestName != "Guest").). The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        policy_name `NewGuestName`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE compliant
        exists boolean = true
        value string != `"Guest"`
        value string != ``
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN windows_security_policy
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF compliant
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
